# The original cPLQ package, kept locally as a reference clone only.
#
# CCA2 contains a substantially REWRITTEN version of that symbolic per-piece machinery (plq.m,
# region.m, functionNDomain.m, symbolicFunction.m and companions, in this repository's root), so
# the original is deliberately NOT bundled. Licensing is not the reason -- cPLQ is GPL-3, same as
# CCA2. The reason is that shipping both would leave users wondering which version to use.
cPLQ/

# Reference papers, kept LOCAL only. These are third-party COPYRIGHTED PDFs and must never ship in
# a public release; CCA2 is private today but is intended to be made public. DESIGN.md and the
# source headers cite them by their [TAG] and filename so the local copies remain findable, but the
# files themselves are not distributed -- see README.md's references section for the full citations,
# which is what a public reader needs.
reference/

# MATLAB / editor cruft
*.asv
*.m~
slprj/

# Published (version-of-record) PDFs of the project's own papers, kept LOCAL only. Same reason as
# reference/ above: redistributing a publisher's typeset version is generally not permitted by the
# publishing agreement, and CCA2 is intended to become public. The papers are cited in full in
# README.md and DESIGN.md ([COAP] and [JOGO]), which is what a public reader needs. The project's
# OWN documents and figures in doc/ (3-edge.tex/.pdf, fig_*.pdf, *.svg) remain tracked.
doc/s10589-026-00781-5.pdf
doc/s10898-025-01503-7.pdf
